# Winamp Tab Chrome Panel Layers

The tab chrome panel (used by Paths, Post Processing) is built from these layers, bottom to top:

## DOM Structure

```
div.win95-panel-section          // outer wrapper (border: none, overflow: hidden in bare mode)
  div.winamp-tab-module          // backing panel (gradient bg, border-radius: 10px, overflow: hidden)
    svg.winamp-tab-fill          // SVG frame (absolute, z-index: 1)
    div.winamp-tab-backplate     // header positioning (absolute, pointer-events: none)
      div.winamp-tab-header-lip  // tab + action buttons container
        span.winamp-folder-tab   // measured by ResizeObserver -> feeds computeTabPanelFrame()
        span.winamp-tab-actions  // action buttons (e.g. import)
    div.winamp-tab-panel         // chrome panel body (children rendered here)
  ::before                       // top shadow gradient (hidden in bare mode)
  ::after                        // rim highlight box-shadows (z-index: 6)
```

## SVG Frame Layers (inside svg.winamp-tab-fill)

Rendered in this order (painter's algorithm):

1. **Shadow group** (`wtf-shadow-group`): 8 concentric strokes around `frame.outline` (strokeWidth 2-7). Clipped by `wtfShadowClipA` (even-odd against `frame.panelRect`) so shadows only paint outside the panel body. Masked by `wtfSideFade` to fade at left/right edges.
2. **Tab fill** (`wtf-tab-fill`): gradient fill for the tab trapezoid above the panel body. Uses `frame.tabFill` path which extends 2px wider than the outline on each side for seamless overlap.
3. **Panel fill** (`wtf-panel-fill`): gradient fill for the panel body rectangle (`frame.panelRect`).
4. **Highlight stroke**: inset white stroke along `frame.highlightPath`, masked by `wtfHighlightFade`.
5. **Outline stroke**: 1px dark border tracing `frame.outline` (the unified tab+panel shape).

## Key Geometry (computeTabPanelFrame)

- Tab width is MEASURED from the `.winamp-folder-tab` DOM element via `getBoundingClientRect()`
- CSS padding on `.winamp-folder-tab` directly controls tab width; SVG adapts automatically
- `TAB_SVG_EXTEND` (6px) widens the SVG tab shape beyond the measured DOM element
- `FLAT_HALF_RATIO` (34/60) controls how much of the tab top is flat vs angled
- **CSS changes require a full page reload** -- the ResizeObserver watches the module, not the tab, so CSS-only HMR doesn't retrigger measurement

## Critical: clipPath uses panelRect, NOT outline

The shadow group clipPath (`wtfShadowClipA`) must use `frame.panelRect` (not `frame.outline`). Using `outline` creates a tab-shaped shadow cutout on the backing panel. The tab fill covers any shadow bleed into the tab area.
